ations is evaluated.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Atom processors': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['Another type of processor on which the performance of sparse CNN implementations is evaluated.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Sparse convolution': {'type': ['method', 'method'], 'description': ['A technique used in sparse CNNs to reduce computational requirements in convolution layers.', 'A method for accelerating CNNs by exploiting sparsity in the convolutional layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1, 2]}, 'Arithmetic intensity': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A factor that affects the performance of sparse convolution, with lower intensity leading to higher overhead.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'CNN': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['Convolutional Neural Network, a type of deep learning model.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Filter Types': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The size of the filters used in the CNN, specifically mentioning small filters like 3x3 and large filters like 9x9.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Images per second throughput': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A performance metric representing the number of images processed per second, indicating the classification speed of a CNN.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Accuracy drop': {'type': ['task'], 'description': ['The change in accuracy when using sparse CNN methods. The text mentions "no accuracy drop" indicating that the sparse method maintains the same accuracy as the dense method.'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}, 'Dense convolution': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The standard convolution operation in CNNs, used as a baseline for comparison with sparse convolution.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'CNNs (Convolutional Neural Networks)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A type of deep learning model, where sparse convolution is applied to improve performance.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Direct sparse convolution algorithm': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['An algorithm presented to advance the state-of-the-art in sparse convolution for speeding up CNNs.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'SpMV (Sparse Matrix-Vector Multiplication)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A computational method that is memory bandwidth bound and used in the context of sparse convolution.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'GEMM (General Matrix Multiplication)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A fundamental linear algebra operation used in the implementation of fully connected layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'SpMDM (Sparse Matrix and Dense Matrix Multiplication)': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A method that can be leveraged for exploiting sparsity in fully connected layers.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Sparse Methods': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['Techniques used to improve classification speed and reduce model size in CNNs by eliminating redundant computations and reducing model size.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Interpolation': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The technique used by Perforated-CNN to handle redundant convolution computations, instead of using sparse methods.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Tensor Lowering and Lifting': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['The process of transforming tensors into matrices (lowering) and back (lifting), which is used in the context of sparse convolution.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Perforated-CNN': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A specific type of Convolutional Neural Network architecture discussed in the text.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'conv2/4_direct': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A specific direct sparse convolution algorithm mentioned in the text.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'conv2/4_lowered': {'type': ['method'], 'description': ['A specific sparse convolution algorithm that operates on tensors lowered to matrices, as described in the text.'], 'source_chunk_index': [2]}, 'Mobile platforms': {'description': ['Resource-constrained devices, such as smartphones, where CNN models are deployed.'], 'type': ['dataset', 'task'], 'source_chunk_index': [0]}, 'Speedup of convolution layers': {'description': ['The performance improvement achieved by the optimized sparse CNN implementation, specifically 3.4x and 7.3x speedups on Xeon and Atom processors, respectively, for convolution layers in AlexNet.', 'The performance improvement achieved in convolution layers, expressed as a multiple (e.g., 3.4x or 7.3x), when using a sparse CNN implementation compared to the best dense direct convolution performance.'], 'type': ['method'], 'source_chunk_index': [1]}}
